137
00:16:07,400 --> 00:16:11,800
Preparation of coating solution for an 8 by 10 inch plate.

138
00:16:12,360 --> 00:16:13,640
Excuse me.

139
00:16:13,960 --> 00:16:20,760
Add 30 grams gelatin to 170 milliliters cold water and mark the liquid level on the beaker.

140
00:16:20,760 --> 00:16:27,640
Place beaker in a water bath and heat while stirring constantly until gelatin solution is between 70 and 80 degrees Celsius.

141
00:16:27,640 --> 00:16:32,920
Stir until all granules have cleared, top up level to the mark.

142
00:16:32,920 --> 00:16:41,640
To remove skin and surface foam, pour through a fine mesh, nylon stockings work fine, into a preheated beaker.

143
00:16:41,640 --> 00:16:48,600
Then immediately proceed to the next step, which is coating by the old Victorian curtain method.

144
00:16:48,600 --> 00:16:57,560
Hold the beaker in your right hand and with your left hand incline the pre-subbed glass plate preheated to around 60 degrees Celsius.

145
00:16:57,560 --> 00:17:03,720
At an angle of about 30 degrees to the vertical with its bottom edge in a clean tray.

146
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:08,440
Pour the gelatin in a line about one centimeter from the top of the plate.

147
00:17:08,440 --> 00:17:14,200
The pouring rate must be continuous until the furthest edge of the plate is reached.

148
00:17:14,200 --> 00:17:23,640
And in parentheses it says you may have to accept the tendency of the coating to not completely cover the lower part closest to the furthest edge.

149
00:17:23,640 --> 00:17:30,680
Lean the plate against something for a few minutes while coating gels.

150
00:17:30,680 --> 00:17:36,440
Run a knife along thick layer at the bottom to free plate rather than risk tearing the delicate coating.

151
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:42,840
I guess uh once you have that uh coated, it becomes thicker, and you don't want to just lift that plate up.

152
00:17:42,840 --> 00:17:49,680
You want to take a little X-acto blade or razor blade or a sharp knife and go along that bottom edge to cut it free.

153
00:17:51,040 --> 00:17:57,680
And in parentheses, since no hardener is involved yet, the gel can be readily scooped up and recoated if you are not satisfied.

154
00:17:57,680 --> 00:17:58,800
Isn't this cool?

155
00:17:58,800 --> 00:17:59,680
Isn't this cool?

